ility depend on qualifications and jurisdiction."},{"type":"h","text":"Mine geology route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mining Graduate","Mine Geology Assistant","Mine Technical Professional","Senior Mine Geology/Exploration Professional","Mine Geology / Technical Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"GIS/resource route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Student","Mining GIS Intern","GIS/Geological Data Technician","Geospatial/Resource Modelling Specialist","Senior Resource Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research / PhD directions"},{"type":"p","text":"Strong research areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mineral exploration"},{"text":"Economic geology"},{"text":"Ore deposit modelling"},{"text":"Critical minerals"},{"text":"Lithium exploration"},{"text":"Rare-earth elements"},{"text":"Copper exploration"},{"text":"Gold deposits"},{"text":"Battery mineral exploration"},{"text":"Geostatistics"},{"text":"3D geological modelling"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Hyperspectral mineral mapping"},{"text":"AI-assisted geological interpretation"},{"text":"Machine-learning-based prospectivity mapping"},{"text":"Automated core logging"},{"text":"Geological computer vision"},{"text":"Sustainable mineral exploration"},{"text":"Mine waste characterization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 career evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Exploration is moving from conventional fieldwork toward integrated digital exploration."},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field mapping","drilling","sampling","laboratory","geological interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"flow","items":["Satellite data","AI prospectivity","geophysics","automated core imaging","3D modelling","resource estimation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Future professionals should therefore understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Drone mapping"},{"text":"Hyperspectral imaging"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Geological databases"},{"text":"3D geological modelling"},{"text":"Geostatistics"},{"text":"Automated core scanning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mining Engineering","Geology","GIS","Data Science","3D Geological Modelling"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Mining"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mining Methods","Drilling","Blasting","Mine Development","Rock Mechanics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Geology"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mineralogy","Petrology","Structural Geology","Economic Geology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Exploration"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mapping","Core Logging","Sampling","Assay QA/QC","Exploration Methods"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"flow","items":["GIS","Remote Sensing","Geological Databases","Excel","Python"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"flow","items":["Geostatistics","3D Geological Modelling","AI-based Exploration"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Reporting","Technical Documentation","Communication","Safety"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Year 1","Mining fundamentals + mineral/rock identification + engineering geology","Year 2","Mineralogy + petrology + structural geology + economic geology","Year 3","Geological mapping + core logging + sampling + GIS + exploration internship","Year 4","Geological modelling + resource concepts + exploration project","First job","Geologist Assistant / Exploration Assistant / Mine Geology Assistant / Exploration Engineer"]},{"type":"h","text":"3–6 years\nExploration Engineer / Geological Technical Professional"},{"type":"h","text":"6–10 years\nSenior Exploration / Resource Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"10–15+ years\nExploration Manager / Technical Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mining Engineering","Applied Geology","Mineral Exploration","GIS","Core Logging","Geological Data"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key distinction is that Mining Engineering alone does not automatically make a graduate eligible for every “Geologist” position. The student should deliberately add geology coursework/field experience and verify the eligibility requirements of each employer or regulated position."}]}]}